Guideline: Use explicit function to choose hash function so cross-chain HTLCs map correctly.

11. Interop & foreign functions
Native host functions (for optimized lower-level behavior) are declared in a host module and can be implemented per-target. Examples:

Host::emit_log(level, bytes)

Host::transfer_native(to: Address, amount: u128)

Host::call_external(chain_id, address, payload) — optional cross-chain RPC

These must be pure specifications in X3, with target backends providing bindings.

