Gas (annotative; compiler uses it)

Type rules

Strong static typing. No implicit integer-width casts. Explicit casts: x as u256.

No floats.

6. Storage model (explicit)
Storage access is explicit through the Storage stdlib — no implicit struct -> storage mapping unless compiler optimization is applied via annotations.

API:

Storage::store_u256(key: Bytes, value: u256)
Storage::load_u256(key: Bytes) -> u256
Storage::store_bytes(key: Bytes, value: Bytes)
Storage::load_bytes(key: Bytes) -> Bytes
Storage::delete(key: Bytes)
Pattern:

Contracts define const SLOT: Bytes = b"token_v1:";

Compute keys deterministically: key_balance(addr) -> concat(SLOT, b"bal:", addr)

Rationale: deterministic layout across backends and safe migrations.

7. Events
Emit events via the Event stdlib:

Event::emit("Transfer", { from: from, to: to, value: amount });
Backends create indexed topics for event fields when possible. Compiler emits ABI event signatures for EVM backend.

8. Functions, visibility & modifiers
Visibility:

pub (external + internal), internal, external, priv (default)

Modifiers: prefer require guards and guard functions; no custom modifier syntax necessary but can be added via @macro in stdlib.

constructor for deployment init. fallback & receive map to EVM only via @target(EVM) annotations.

9. Control flow & operators
Core operators (ordered for readability — compiler implements precedence table):

Arithmetic: + - * / % **

Bitwise: & | ^ << >> ~

Comparison: < > <= >= == !=

Logical: && || !

Ternary: cond ? a : b

Assignment & compound: =, +=, -=, *=, /=, %=, <<=

We keep precedence conventional; compiler provides full precedence table (same as common languages). No ambiguous packed encoding ops in core.

10. Error handling & assertions
require(cond, "message") -> revert-like (user-facing errors)

assert(cond) -> internal invariant (panic-like)

revert("message")

try/catch for external calls where backend supports (EVM: low-level call patterns)

Error values: Result<T,E> optional pattern for library-level errors.

11. Gas metering
Compiler inserts gas checks — each function has an implicit gas_left() check. IR annotation:

Gas cost per op documented in stdlib

Loops add per-iteration metering

gas_left() available

refund_gas(amount) hint (backend may ignore)

Rationale: keep gas model backend-specific but predictable at IR level.

